WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Welcome to Basecamp.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.666
Basecamp is a place for you to keep all the work and discussions that go into completing projects.

3
00:00:06.666 --> 00:00:10.633
No more long, unnecessary meetings or unwieldly email chains.

4
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:19.500
All your discussions, tasks, files, and important dates regarding that project are in Basecamp and can be accessed anytime by anyone else on the project.

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.266
The discussion section of your project is where you can post updates, upload files, and give feedback on the work.

6
00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:32.533
When posting a new message or commenting on an existing thread you can also decide who you would like to notify about the update.

7
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:41.500
Everyone with access to the thread can still log in and see what you've written, but only those who you've chosen to notify will get an email alerting them to your message.

8
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.533
These email notifications are super-handy.

9
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:56.233
Not only are they a great way to stay up to date on the project, but anytime you get notified a change like a new message or file you can reply directly to that email and your response will automatically be added to Basecamp.

10
00:00:56.233 --> 00:00:58.500
You don't even need to log in.

11
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.266
Basecamp is also a great place to share files.

12
00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:06.333
You can attach files to a discussion or upload them on their own just by dragging them from your desktop.

13
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:09.900
Once you post a file people can then add any comments they wish.

14
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.366
New versions of files can also be added to the thread.

15
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:17.200
Clicking on a file icon or thumbnail will let you preview and download it if you wish.

16
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.033
Well, that's the basics.

17
00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:24.900
For more detailed guides and tutorials come visit us at basecamp.com/help
